# Playwright E2E

Write critical user flows (login, checkout, navigation), not visual CSS checks. Locators and Page Object Model stay in `qa-playwright-standards.mdc`.

## Structure

- Put UI specs in `tests/ui/` and API specs in `tests/api/`.
- Group related cases with `test.describe`.
- Put shared navigation and route stubs in `test.beforeEach`.
- Use names that state the behavior: `should show an error for invalid credentials`.
- Keep a file to about 3–5 focused tests. Cover the happy path and at least one failure path.

## Waiting and assertions

- Use Playwright auto-wait and web-first assertions (`toBeVisible`, `toHaveURL`, `toHaveText`).
- Never use `page.waitForTimeout`. Do not assert `isVisible()` without `expect`.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
await page.waitForTimeout(2000);
expect(await page.getByText('Welcome').isVisible()).toBe(true);

// ✅ GOOD
await expect(page.getByText('Welcome')).toBeVisible();
```

## Isolation

- Prefer the real app when the flow needs it. Use `page.route` only to stub flaky or external APIs so the UI test stays deterministic.
- Do not assert colors, fonts, or pixel layout. Assert user-visible outcomes.
